"In Renjen-art'h's era, training facilities raised children to be bound, with no care for suitability."
"They taught knighthood as the only decent life, allowed little outside contact, and bound children early."
"Hundreds of thousands were churned through them."
"Renjen, among the most powerful Artonans ever, sired at least sixteen hundred children to fill them."
"The Primary, Alis and Tesen were among his last, raised in the art'h dormitory by the mleirt Murmur."
"Survivors of that generation find it repulsive; oaths and choosing seasons are what they lacked."
"Now the lives of young knights are held precious."
